  "Question": "For \\(x = 7,\\) which of the following is the smallest?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{6}{x} \\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{6}{x+1} \\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{6}{x-1} \\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{x}{6} \\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{x+1}{6} \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Substituting \\(x=7\\), the five choices become\n\\[\n\\frac67,\\quad \\frac68,\\quad 1,\\quad \\frac76,\\quad \\frac86.\n\\]\nThe last two are greater than \\(1\\), while the first two are less than \\(1\\). Of the fractions \\(6/7\\) and \\(6/8\\), the one with the larger denominator is smaller because both have the same positive numerator. Thus the smallest value is \\(\\boxed{\\frac68=\\frac34}\\), choice B.",
